Short: Fido-MSG-Base Reader/Writer (Foozle compatible) works w. StdIn/StdOut
Type: comm/bbs
Version: V1.3

This package allows sysops to include their Foozle (or compatible) -
Tosser styled messagebases into the BBS. All you need is a tosser that
uses *.MSG style messagebases and a BBS that runs doors via StdIn/StdOut.

The user can browse through the given message-directory, read single
messages, reply to them in echo or via NetMail - or of course post a
message himself. A *.MSG-File is generated according to Foozle.techref
so all the sysop has to do after calling MSGRead is to rescan the used
area and export.

V1.1 is an update that fixes two major bugs:
     - origin, tearline etc. are no longer converted to lower case
     - origin does not "start" with a NULL - sorry 'bout that!

V1.2 is an update with some memory bugfixes
V1.3 has improved Break-Handling
